cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TokenTaint, please cite it as below."
title: "TokenTaint: A Provenance-Tracking Firewall for LLM Agent Prompt Injection"
authors:
  - family-names: "Choksi"
    given-names: "Krishita Sanjay"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-08-22
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Krishita17/TokenTaint"
keywords:
  - prompt injection
  - LLM agent security
  - taint analysis
  - information-flow control
abstract: >
  TokenTaint defends LLM agents against prompt injection by labeling every span
  of the context window with its source of trust, propagating that taint through
  the agent's reasoning, and refusing to let a privileged tool ("sink") fire when
  its justification traces to an untrusted origin — a structural guarantee that
  does not depend on recognizing the injection's phrasing.
